Well... after playing for a while today... and yesterday...
I've come to the conclusion that it really sucks to play
on Friday the 13th when there is a full moon.
The full moon I can handle... but combine the two and its
horrid!

Anyone look up exactly what happens on Friday the 13th?

Things I noticed...

 o God seams to start off annoyed at you... so praying is out until
   you've sacrificed a few monsters at an altar.
 o There seem to be an overabundance of violet gems. (don't ask me,
   these are just things I noticed)
 o Were-critters up the ying yang! (and combined with the inability to
   pray as per the first point, makes for ALOT of deaths due to being
   a rat or jackel)
 o Monsters seem to be randomly generated quicker.
 o seem to be alot more traps laying about.

Now, I'm not sure if any of these are actual features, or just my
imagination, but a played a fair number of games today, and I noticed
these points on all of them (especially the damn violet gem one...
they were all over the place in all the games!)

Anyway, just curious.

